<newsitem itemid="619664" id="root" date="1997-05-28" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Metcash lifts yr headline EPS 25 percent.</title>
<headline>Metcash lifts yr headline EPS 25 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended April 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		17.0	  vs    13.6</p>
<p>    - attrib		  17.1	  vs    13.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  7.0	  vs     5.6</p>
<p>    Attrib income	  156.35	 vs   115.78</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  247.80	 vs   190.62</p>
<p>    Tax			 81.03	 vs    72.62</p>
<p>    Net interest income   53.33	 vs    42.98</p>
<p>    Turnover	     8,981.21	 vs 7,580.43</p>
<p>Full name: Metro Cash and Carry Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast Metcash's headline earnings per share for the year at 17.1 cents and its dividend at seven cents.</p>
<p>Metcash said it would award capitalisation shares to shareholders registered on or before June 9. Shareholders would be able to receive a four cent cash dividend instead of the shares, it said.</p>
<p>Metcash implemented a five-for-one share split in the year under review. Year ago figures have been adjusted accordingly.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
